# Line endings are not cosmetic here — two files in this repo break outright
# with the wrong ones, so they are pinned rather than left to each developer's
# core.autocrlf setting.
#
#   run.cmd  MUST be CRLF. cmd.exe mis-parses an LF-only batch file: REM lines
#            get truncated mid-token and surface as "'M' is not recognized as
#            an internal or external command". Observed, not theoretical.
#   run.sh   MUST be LF. A shebang line ending in CR makes the kernel look for
#            an interpreter literally named "bash\r", which does not exist.
#            Same for anything that runs inside the Linux containers.

# Let Git decide what is text, and normalize to LF in the repository.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts: checked out with CRLF everywhere.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Scripts that run under a shell — including inside Docker images built from
# this repo — must keep LF even when checked out on Windows.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf

# Binary files Git should never try to normalize.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
